{
  "info": {
    "name": "Enterprise Payment Platform - Phase 4 API Tests",
    "description": "Phase 4 API acceptance collection. Run sequentially. Authentication flows use CUSTOMER token; privileged requests require operationsToken. Negative cases assert stable ApiError codes. Dependency-outage scenarios are documented in docs/verification/phase-4-complete-testing-guide.md and must be executed only in a disposable local environment.\n\nRole test order: Login as OPERATIONS and Login as ADMIN in the Privileged role authentication folder. Tokens are stored separately as operationsToken and adminToken. The reconciliation discrepancies request is a root-level request immediately after the Role authorization folder.\n\nFeature-oriented folders: Authentication and JWT; Privileged role authentication; Role authorization (privileged token optional); Reconciliation; Redis rate limiting. Reconciliation endpoints are grouped in Reconciliation rather than the generic role-authorization folder.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
